    <briefdescription>
<para>Latency measurement result published to the switchboard. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This structure contains the measured network latency and related statistics that other plugins can consume. This is published locally (not over network).</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>The directional latencies (client_to_server_ms and server_to_client_ms) are only accurate if the client and server clocks are synchronized (e.g., via NTP or PTP). Without synchronization, these values will include clock offset and may even be negative.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>The estimated_clock_offset_ms assumes symmetric network latency. Positive values mean the server clock is ahead of the client clock. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
